# Rotational / Upper Power

Throws are ballistic — the implement leaves your hands, so there is no braking
phase and the movement stays at max velocity through the finish. Cable and
landmine work forces you to decelerate before end range, so peak velocity is
capped. **Take the throws when the gym allows it**; the cable / landmine
sub-group is the fallback, run at slightly higher reps.

Overhead Slam and Rotational Slam need only a slam ball and a floor — no wall,
no bounce — so they often survive when the wall throws don't.

### Throws

* Rotational Throw
* Side Toss
* Step-behind Throw
* Chest Pass
* Shot Put Throw
* Overhead Slam
* Rotational Slam
* Scoop Toss
* Backward Throw

### Cable / Landmine

